ins anchored in base prompts. `PROMPT_light.md` directly implements the chaining side through its chaining/routing note and staged-path rules. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` reinforces the ownership boundary by saying advanced prompting, chaining-shaped, and routing-shaped examples are exemplars only, not activation or execution owners. This means the bundle does not depend on operator-only guides to answer the question, and it does not require assembled replay for this document-parity judgment because `CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` also says document-level benchmark is the primary sufficient surface for runtime owner integrity and that replay escalation is not required unless the claim moves into behavior proof or runner state. The bundle also stays bounded: `AGENTS.md` and `PROMPT_light.md` both prefer the lightest sufficient path and reject decorative orchestration, so there is no sign of unnecessary multi-agent escalation or patch widening for this scenario.","limitations":["Limitation: The active bundle directly proves runtime carryover and ownership boundaries, but it does not by itself prove family-by-family completeness against any out-of-scope external Appendix A source text beyond the explicitly named advanced prompting families.","Limitation: `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` supports this verdict only as a boundary document; its advanced-prompting and chaining entries are not independent execution owners."]}
